;; Our notes on SRD rules, in our own words: not SRD text, and not covered by the SRD's licence.
;; Each one says what an official ruling holds and links where Wizards published it. Shown after
;; the rule it clarifies on the Rules pages (srd-improvements.md, "Rules clarifications").
{:notes
 [{:section :attacking
   :anchor :rolling-1-or-20
   :title "Spell attacks can be critical hits"
   :text "A spell that makes an attack roll scores a critical hit on a 20 like any other attack: the critical hit rule covers every attack roll, from a weapon or a spell."
   :source {:name "Sage Advice Compendium (v1.01)"
            :url "https://media.wizards.com/2015/downloads/dnd/SA_Compendium_1.01.pdf"}}
  {:section :combat-sequence
   :anchor :bonus-actions
   :title "Actions and bonus actions don't trade"
   :text "You can't spend your action on something that takes a bonus action, or the other way round. A bard who grants Bardic Inspiration with their bonus action can't also cast healing word, which takes a bonus action too, by spending their action on it."
   :source {:name "Sage Advice Compendium (v1.01)"
            :url "https://media.wizards.com/2015/downloads/dnd/SA_Compendium_1.01.pdf"}}]}
